  "id": "behavioral-pharmacology",
  "term": "behavioral pharmacology",
  "definition": "Behavioral pharmacology is a translational research area that uses behavioral models, often in animals, to study drug-related effects in relation to behavior. It is used to help identify treatment targets and to examine the neurobehavioral basis of disorders and possible treatments.",
